/**
 * NextKey — translations.
 *
 * English is NOT here. It lives in index.html, demo.html and try.html
 * themselves, so each page is complete and readable before a single line of
 * script runs, and a JavaScript failure degrades to English rather than to a
 * blank document. Keeping a second English copy in this file would only give
 * the two a chance to drift, and the one that drifts is always the one nobody
 * reads.
 *
 * Each entry is applied over the DOM by key. A missing key falls back to the
 * English original for that one string, so a partial translation costs a
 * sentence rather than a page.
 *
 * Keys are prefixed by page: no prefix for the landing page, `d.` for the live
 * view, `t.` for the hands-on page. A few `t.` keys are also read from
 * src/try.js, for strings that only exist after a button has been pressed and
 * so cannot be tagged in the HTML.
 *
 * A handful of values contain markup (how.2p, hood.1p, faq.6a1, t.after1,
 * t.nojs, t.warn1) and are inserted as HTML. Their attributes use single or
 * escaped quotes; nothing here is user input.
 *
 * fa is right-to-left. Each page sets dir="rtl" for it. The landing page's
 * handover diagram deliberately stays left-to-right, because it depicts a
 * sequence of events rather than a line of text; on try.html the step numbers
 * mirror, because a numbered list is a line of text.
 */
